    {
      "id": "un3zu1j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "17. HIGH-PROBABILITY SSC RULES"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Never use double modals together in a single clause (e.g., incorrect: 'He should can do this').",
        "Avoid using 'to' after main modals like Can, Could, May, Might, Shall, Will, Should, Must (e.g., write 'Can do', not 'Can to do').",
        "When 'Need' or 'Dare' acts as a modal in negative sentences, use bare infinitive without 'to' (e.g., 'He need not go', NOT 'He need not to go').",
        "Pay attention to 'Should have + V3' which signifies an action that ought to have happened in the past but did not."
      ],
      "id": "pflzfa4"
    },
